#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Render final measurements from audited selections, never from live snapshots."""
import json,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);f=root/'analysis/final'
s=json.loads((f/'selected-results.json').read_text());counts=json.loads((f/'counts.json').read_text());paired=json.loads((root/'analysis/paired/paired-startup.json').read_text());proof=json.loads((f/'evidence-verification.json').read_text())
perf={(r['host'],r['tool'],r['case']):r for r in s['performance']}
lines=['# Remaining startup overhead and Pi writes','', 'The final patch reduces Linux startup while retaining fresh capability checks, strict observation and empty-tree settlement. The source baseline is ac1263a; it already contains the earlier file-denial fix. The original and first-after datasets remain unchanged.','', '## Matched startup comparison','', 'No-op wall medians, milliseconds; 30 valid samples per arm on each host. Paired reductions use the median of within-round ratios, which differs from the ratio of column medians.','', '| Host | Before | After | Paired reduction | Paired change 95% interval | MXC | Greywall |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
details=[]
for host in ['vps','pi']:
 r=next(r for r in paired['comparisons'] if r['host']==host and r['case']=='noop');m=perf[host,'mxc','noop']['elapsed_ms']['median'];g=perf[host,'greywall','noop']['elapsed_ms']['median']
 lines.append(f"| {host.upper()} | {r['old_median_ms']:.1f} | {r['after_median_ms']:.1f} | {r['paired_median_reduction_percent']:.1f}% | [{r['paired_delta_ci95_low_ms']:.1f}, {r['paired_delta_ci95_high_ms']:.1f}] ms | {m:.1f} | {g:.1f} |")
 details.append(f"On {host}, the remaining median gap to MXC is {r['after_median_ms']-m:.1f} ms ({r['after_median_ms']/m:.1f}x its elapsed time), versus {r['old_median_ms']-m:.1f} ms before. Greywall takes {g/r['after_median_ms']:.1f}x Ouro's elapsed time in this lane.")
lines += ['', *details]
lines+=['','[All seven paired workloads, medians, tails and intervals](analysis/paired/paired-startup.csv), [all native/container performance cells](analysis/final/performance.csv). Bootstrap intervals use 10,000 round-pair resamples and seed 20261011; they are descriptive, with no multiple-test correction.','', 'All 840 scored old/new Ouro samples retain matching policy digests, enforced containment, strict observation, attached ptrace/linux-closed-v1, unchanged declared coverage, no gaps and empty-tree settlement. Each of the 120 write samples records all 1,000 fs.write observations. Fresh doctor status/reason/mechanism rows and paired syscall/safety checks match.','', 'The Pi Git p95 rises from 459.3 to 475.8 ms despite a lower median; no universal tail-latency improvement is claimed.', '', '## What changed','', '- Ordinary unprotected DT_REG entries avoid redundant metadata queries. Protected names, directories, symlinks and unknown types still receive no-follow stat; bounds, directory stamps, inode pins and mount-handoff checks remain. Parent-only profiles remove roughly 2,000 queries from the standard fixture.','- Namespace, read-only-bind and baseline-filter checks share one fresh successful sandbox. Every independent validator must succeed; unsuccessful combinations fall back to the prior unfiltered/individual paths. There is no persistent capability cache.','- Boundary fields are read from one blocked-launcher /proc/status snapshot. Missing CapEff explicitly refuses. Observer shutdown wakes on events/channel closure, still draining and joining for the final account.','- A candidate cached backend-version optimization was withdrawn to retain fresh receipt readback in long-lived processes. Its complete/partial measurements and interruption records remain in [candidate evidence](candidates/v3/README.md), excluded from final comparisons.','', '## Pi writes','', 'The direct control spends about 805 ms closing just-truncated files, versus about 2 ms when overwriting without truncation or creating fresh files. Writes themselves take about 13 ms. The SD/ext4 close hotspot also appears without Ouro; it is not established as an Ouro-specific regression.','', '[Pi investigation](PI-WRITES.md) separates observed facts from the inferred ext4 allocation/writeback explanation. The diagnostic variants change semantics and are excluded. Original O_TRUNC work, storage, governor, mount options, durability requirements and observation policy stay unchanged.','', '| Host | Write before median | After median | Paired change 95% interval |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for host in ['vps','pi']:
 r=next(r for r in paired['comparisons'] if r['host']==host and r['case']=='writes');lines.append(f"| {host.upper()} | {r['old_median_ms']:.1f} ms | {r['after_median_ms']:.1f} ms | [{r['paired_delta_ci95_low_ms']:.1f}, {r['paired_delta_ci95_high_ms']:.1f}] ms |")
lines+=['','## Coding and container rerun','',f"The final protocol retains {counts['native_invocations']} native small-task calls, {counts['container_invocations']} container small-task calls and {counts['workflow_invocations']} inventory workflows. There are {counts['valid_performance_samples']} valid timing samples in {counts['performance_buckets']} cells. Failed attempts remain in the raw data. Models, client/product versions, prompts, task checks, limits and schedules are unchanged.",'','| Native product | Linux small tasks | Linux workflows | Mac small tasks | Mac workflows |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for mode in ['ouro','mxc','greywall','direct']:
 row=[mode]
 for hosts,kind in [(['vps','pi'],'small'),(['vps','pi'],'workflow'),(['mac'],'small'),(['mac'],'workflow')]:
  if mode=='ouro' and hosts==['mac']:row.append('unavailable');continue
  if kind=='small':
   a=[r for r in s['native_agents'] if r['host'] in hosts and r['mode']==mode];row.append(f"{sum(r['passed'] for r in a)}/{sum(r['attempted'] for r in a)}")
  else:
   a=[r for r in s['workflows'] if r['kind']=='native' and r['host'] in hosts and r['mode']==mode];row.append(f"{sum(r['success'] for r in a)}/{len(a)}")
 lines.append('| '+' | '.join(row)+' |')
lines+=['','[Native coding calls](analysis/final/native-agents.csv), [container coding calls](analysis/final/container-agents.csv), [all workflows](analysis/final/workflows.csv), [before/after coding observation](analysis/final/coding-observation-before-after.json). Model/provider elapsed times and individual coding failures are compatibility evidence, not clean sandbox CPU measurements.','', 'One retained OpenShell/Codex Mac call failed because the selected model was at capacity; it was neither retried nor switched to another model. Mac container small tasks pass 53/54 and workflows 9/9. Greywall Mac Seatbelt and MXC Mac Codex CFPreferences failures remain visible.','', 'Fresh/retained containers are separate lifecycle classes with matched Docker controls. OpenShell images are reused exactly on Mac/Pi; deleted VPS client images are reconstructed in owned new tags with unchanged client bytes and recipe, and removed only after their evidence is retained. Full IDs, build logs, policies and inputs are saved.','', '## Where Ouro leads and trails','', '- Ouro launches substantially faster than Greywall in the measured Linux wrapper lane. Strict receipts and journals expose policy, executable identity, containment, coverage/loss and process-tree settlement. Tested memory limits refuse on the Pi when enforcement is unavailable; normal containment/observer settings remain intact.','- MXC still has lower native startup cost. These interfaces do not deliver identical evidence surfaces, so the latency result is not a claim of equal audit behavior. Other optional competitor audit backends were not measured.','- OpenShell offers working retained containers and online Mac execution. Ouro has no native Mac agent lane in this comparison; its offline Mac VM preview is a separate diagnostic. OpenShell startup fails on the Pi, while native Ouro runs there. Fresh container creation and retained exec are not mixed into wrapper rankings.','- Linux agent compatibility is largely shared with the working competitors. Provider capacity and turn-limit outcomes do not establish that a jail improves model intelligence. Ouro vault/provider brokerage and competitor privileged audit options remain untested.','- Tested file-denial and network/resource behavior is retained. Greywall rule-precedence follow-ups include the alternative working minimal rules; visible-socket IPC policy differences are not described as sandbox escapes.','', '## Validation and reuse','', 'Rust 1.98.1 release builds use opt-level 3. Clippy and 565 Linux unit tests per host pass. The VPS passes all 206 exercised observer/isolation integration tests and both new mechanism regressions. On the Pi, broader suites retain confirmed baseline host/architecture, slow-consumer and queue-pressure failures; no assertion, queue limit or host restriction was relaxed. These are not a fresh pinned reference-host job or release freeze.','', '[Evidence verification](analysis/final/evidence-verification.json), [protocol](METHODS.md), [final source patch](source.patch), [source hashes](source-files.json), [binary hashes](analysis/binaries.json), [full raw artifacts](results/), [archives](archives/), and SHA256SUMS bind the saved results. Credentials, private proxy stores, agent homes and CA private keys are excluded/redacted; exact-value and pattern audits precede packaging. Every referenced final Ouro journal is retained and verified.','', 'The changes and artifacts are uncommitted in the working tree. No release or deployment is claimed.']
(root/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
